hadiths[44]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1776","It is narrated from Ibn Shihab that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Give precedence to the Quraysh and do not put yourselves before them; learn from them and do not compete with them in knowledge, or do not teach them."" Ibn Abi Fudayk is uncertain about these words."
"1777","It is narrated from Hakeem bin Abi Hakeem that he heard from Umar bin Abdul Aziz and Ibn Shihab, both of whom said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever disgraces the Quraysh, Allah Almighty will disgrace him."""
"1778","It is narrated from Harith bin Abdur Rahman, he said: It has reached us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""If the Quraysh had not been ungrateful (and arrogant), I would have told them what (blessings) Allah has for them."""
"1779","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said regarding the Quraysh: ""You are the most deserving of this matter (caliphate) among the people as long as you adhere to the truth, except if you turn away from it, then you will be separated from it just as the bark is separated from the branch of this date-palm."" The Prophet (ﷺ) was pointing to the date-palm branch he was holding in his hand."
"1780","It is narrated from Rifaa Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ called out: ""O people! The Quraysh are the trustees (of leadership, imamate, caliphate). Whoever finds fault with them or rebels against them, Allah Almighty will cast him down on his face (into Hell)."" The Prophet ﷺ repeated these words three times."
"1781","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Harith Taimi that Qatadah bin Nu’man (may Allah be pleased with him) said some harsh words about the Quraysh (it seemed as if he had been hurt by them). So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Qatadah! Stop, be patient, do not speak ill of the Quraysh, for indeed, perhaps you will see among them such people that, compared to their deeds, you will consider your own deeds insignificant, and compared to their actions, you will consider your own actions few, and when you see them, you will envy them. If the Quraysh had not shown arrogance (ingratitude), I would have told them what Allah has in store for them (in Paradise).”"
"1782","It is narrated from Ibn Abi Dhi’b (he mentioned the chain of narration but I could not remember it) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something good about the Quraysh (which I could not remember), and said: ""Even the bad people of Quraysh are like the good people among (other) bad people."""
"1783","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was drawing water from a well (standing and pulling up a bucket)."" (Imam Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: That is, in a dream, and the dreams of the Prophets (peace be upon them) are also revelation.) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then Ibn Abi Quhafa (Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him) came and he drew one or two buckets, and there was some weakness (a short duration) in his drawing; may Allah forgive him. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came and he drew (the bucket) until it became a large bucket in his hand, and the people watered their camels from the pool, and I have not seen a strong man like him who could work as hard as he did."""
"1784","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If it were not for the virtue of migration, I would have preferred to be one of the Ansar, and if people were to walk in a valley or a mountain pass, I would walk in the valley or mountain pass of the Ansar."" (That is, I would prefer to be with them.)"
"1785","It is narrated from Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out during his (last) illness and delivered a sermon. He praised and glorified Allah, then said: ""The Ansar have fulfilled the responsibilities that were upon them, and their reward is still due upon you. Therefore, appreciate the good deeds of their virtuous ones and overlook the mistakes of their wrongdoers."" Jurjani, in his narration, said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Forgive the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."" And in his narration, he said that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came out, the women and children of the Ansar gathered around him, so he showed kindness to them, then delivered a sermon and said these things."
"1786","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, Zubair, and Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with them) and said: When you reach Rawdat Khakh (the name of a place), there you will find an old woman (riding a camel), she will have a letter with her. We set out, and our horses were swiftly carrying us until we reached that old woman. We said to her, “Take out the letter!” She said, “I have no letter.” We said to her again, “Take out the letter, or we will strip you of your clothes.” So she took out the letter from her hair braid, and we brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Its contents were: from Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah to some men among the polytheists of Makkah, informing them in that letter of some matters (secrets) of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, “O Hatib! What is this?” He said, “Do not be hasty in judging me. My situation was that I chose to stay among the Quraysh, and I had no kinship with them, while the other Muhajirun with you have relatives among them, so (the people of Makkah) protect and support their relatives and property because of those ties. I had no kinship with the people of Makkah, so I wanted, since I had no kinship with them, to do them a favor (so that in return they would protect my relatives). By Allah! I did not do this out of doubt in my religion, nor out of being pleased with disbelief after Islam.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (after hearing his words): “He has spoken the truth.” Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), allow me to strike the neck of this hypocrite.” But the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “He participated in the Battle of Badr (with the Muslims), and you do not know, Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: ‘Do whatever you wish, I have forgiven you.’” And then this verse was revealed: “O you who believe! Do not take My enemies and your enemies as friends, offering them love...” (Al-Mumtahanah: 1) __QUR_N__ __XREF_N__ __REF_N__"
"1787","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: On the day of Hudaybiyyah, our number was 1400, and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Today you are the best among all the people of the world."" Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""If I had eyesight today, I would show you the place of that tree."""
"1788","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) stood to deliver a sermon at Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood among us just as I am standing, and he (ﷺ) said: “Honor my companions, then those who are close to them (the Followers), then those who are close to them (the Followers of the Followers). Then falsehood will become widespread to the extent that a person will swear an oath without being asked to do so, and he will bear witness without being asked to bear witness. Beware! Whoever wishes to reside in the middle part of Paradise should remain with the congregation, for indeed Satan is with the one who is alone, while he is farther from two people (because of their unity). And no man should be alone with a non-mahram woman, for Satan is the third among them. And whoever is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his bad deed, then he is a believer.”"
"1789","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Yemen will come to you; they are soft-hearted, and the coverings of their hearts are delicate. Faith is of the Yemenis, and wisdom is also of the Yemenis."""
"1790","Hasan bin Qasim Al-Azraq narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the mountain pass of Tabuk and said: ""There is misfortune here."" And he ﷺ pointed with his hand towards Sham and said: ""And there is blessing here."" And he ﷺ pointed with his hand towards Madinah."
"1791","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that Tufail bin Amr Dausi (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah! The (tribe of) Daus has not obeyed and has refused to listen to the word of Allah, so please invoke a curse upon them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned his face towards the Qiblah and raised his hands, so the noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) thought that now the people of Daus would be destroyed. But the Prophet ﷺ prayed: ""O Allah! Guide the people of Daus and bring them (to Islam)."""
"1792","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will find people (in good and bad) like mines of gold and silver; those who were the best among them in the pre-Islamic period are the best in Islam as well, provided they gain understanding of the religion."""
"1793","Saeed bin Jubair (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that I said to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Nauf Bikali claims that the companion of Khidr, Musa (peace be upon him), was not Musa (peace be upon him) of Bani Israel."" So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""By Allah! The enemy of Allah has lied."" Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) told me, he said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon to us, then he (ﷺ) narrated the long hadith about the incident of Musa and Khidr, which indicates that Musa (the Prophet, peace be upon him) was indeed the companion of Khidr."
"1794","It is narrated from Abu Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I should not find any one of you reclining on his couch, and when a command of mine comes to him, whether I have ordered something or forbidden something, he says: ‘I do not know; we will follow only what we find in Allah’s Book.’”"
"1795","Sufyan (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us, he said: Muhammad bin Munkadir (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to me this same hadith as mursal from the Prophet ﷺ. Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: By ""al-areekah"" is meant ""sarir"" (bed/couch)."
"1796","Abu Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I should not find any one of you reclining on his couch, and when a command of mine comes to him, whether I have ordered something or forbidden something, he says: ‘We do not know; we will follow only what we find in the Book of Allah.’”"
"1797","Ibn Uyaynah (may Allah have mercy on him) reported with a chain that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""People should not cling to my words, for I declare lawful only that which Allah has made lawful for them, and I declare unlawful only that which Allah has made unlawful for them."""
"1798","It is narrated from Amr bin Abu Amr, the freed slave of Matlib bin Hatab, that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""I have not left anything that Allah has commanded you to do except that I have commanded you to do it, and I have not left anything that Allah has forbidden you from except that I have also forbidden you from it. And indeed, the Trustworthy Spirit (Jibreel عليه السلام) has inspired this into my heart: when death comes to anyone, his sustenance has already been completed. Therefore, do not strive for the world with a broken heart."""
"1799","Aamir bin Sa’d narrated from his father that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the greatest offender among the Muslims is the one who asked about something that was not forbidden, and because of his question, it was made forbidden.”"
"1800","Through another chain, from 'Amir bin Sa'd from his father, a narration with the same meaning as the previous hadith is reported from the Prophet ﷺ."
"1801","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever (matter) I have left for you, then leave me in that as well, for the nations before you were destroyed because of their excessive (unnecessary) questioning and their disagreements with their prophets. And whatever I command you to do, do as much of it as you are able, and whatever I forbid you from, then abstain from it."""
"1802","Through another chain, a narration with the same meaning as the previous hadith is reported from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"1803","Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was constantly asked about the Hour until Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: ""What concern is it of yours to declare it?"" (Surah An-Nazi'at: 43)."
"1804","Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""I pledged allegiance to the Prophet (ﷺ) to be sincere to every Muslim."""
"1805","Tamim Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Religion is the name of sincerity."" Religion is the name of being sincere: to Allah, to His Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), to the leaders of the Muslims, and to the common Muslims."""
"1806","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah keep fresh the face of that servant who heard my words, preserved them, remembered them, and conveyed them to others. For sometimes the bearer of knowledge is not himself a jurist (i.e., does not possess the ability of deduction), and sometimes the bearer of knowledge conveys it to one who is more of a jurist than himself. There are three qualities in which the heart of a Muslim does not betray (i.e., a Muslim adopts them wholeheartedly): acting sincerely for the sake of Allah, wishing well for the Muslims, and remaining attached to the community of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses them from behind."""
"1807","It is narrated from Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The greatest slander is that someone attributes to me something which I did not say, or that someone claims to have seen in a dream what he did not see (i.e., narrates a false dream), and that someone claims someone other than his father as his father.”"
"1808","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes to me something that I did not say, let him make his abode in Hell."""
"1809","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he ﷺ said: ""Whoever attributes a lie to me, a house will be built for him in Hell."""
"1810","It is narrated from Asid bin Abi Asid, who narrates from his mother, that she asked Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him): ""What is it with you that you do not narrate hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as others do?"" She says that Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me, let him prepare his place in the Hellfire."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying this while moving his hand on the ground."
"1811","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Relate (incidents) from the Children of Israel, there is no harm in it, and narrate hadiths from me, but do not attribute lies to me."""
"1812","Hisham bin Urwah narrated from his father that he said: ""Sometimes I hear a hadith and I like it, but I do not narrate it because someone who hears it might act upon it, while I have heard it from a person whom I do not consider reliable, even though he has narrated it from someone whom I do consider reliable. And sometimes I hear it from a trustworthy person while he is narrating it from someone who is not trustworthy."" Sa‘d bin Ibrahim said: ""No one should narrate hadiths from the Prophet ﷺ except trustworthy narrators."""
"1813","Yahya bin Saeed narrated that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) was asked about an issue, but he did not give any answer. Then it was said to him: ""We find it very (strange) that you are the son of two rightly guided Imams (i.e., Umar and Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them), and you are asked about an issue while you do not have knowledge about it?"" So he replied: ""An even stranger thing in the sight of Allah, and for the one who recognizes Allah, and for the one who has understanding from Allah, is that I should say something about which I have no knowledge, or that I should narrate something from an unreliable (narrator)."""
"1814","Muhammad bin Idris (Shafi'i), may Allah have mercy on him, said: ""I have narrated mursal ahadith from the Prophet ﷺ regarding punishments and the determination of their times, but we have abandoned them only because of their being disconnected."""
"1815","Rabi’ said: I heard Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) say: Imam Abu Hanifa (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked about a fasting person who eats, drinks, and has intercourse until the break of dawn (what is the ruling on this?). There was a respected man sitting with him who said: “What do you think if dawn breaks in the middle of the night?” So he (may Allah have mercy on him) said: “O lame one! Be silent.”"
"1816","I heard from Rabi' bin Sulayman, who says: I heard from Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him), who said: ""Acquiring knowledge is better than voluntary prayer."""
"1817","Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: “If it were not for Imam Malik and Sufyan, may Allah have mercy on them both, knowledge would have been taken away from Hijaz.”"
"1818","Asam said: I heard from Rabi’ bin Sulayman, when Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, said «اخبرني من لا اتهم» , he meant Ibrahim bin Abu Yahya, and when he said «اخبرني الثقة» , he meant Yahya bin Hassan."
"1819","Asam said: I heard from Rabee’, he said: Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, passed away on the last day of Rajab in the year 204 Hijri, and when he was asked about his age, he said: “Fifty years and a little more.”"
